      "Ability§To Strike Down the Unclean Behemoths": {
        "text": "While this Chivalric Quest is active, add 1 to its tally each time a MONSTER or VEHICLE unit is destroyed by an attack made by an IMPERIAL KNIGHTS model from your Crusade force. For each of those detroyed units that was TITANIC, you gain 1 additional tally mark."
      },
      "Ability§To Raise High the Pennants of Victory": {
        "text": "While this Chivalric Quest is active, at the end of each battle, add 1 to its tally for each objective marker you control. For each of those objective markers that is within your opponent’s deployment zone, you gain 1 additional tally mark."
      },
      "Ability§To Stamp Out the Champions of Dishonour": {
        "text": "While this Chivalric Quest is active, add 1 to its tally each time a CHARACTER unit is destroyed by an attack made by an IMPERIAL KNIGHTS model from your Crusade force. For each of those detroyed units that was your opponent’s WARLORD, you gain 1 additional tally mark."
      },
      "Ability§To Secure the Realm": {
        "text": "While this Chivalric Quest is active, al the end of each battle, add 1 to its tally for each of the following conditions you satisfy: one or more IMPERIAL KNIGHTS units from your Crusade army are within 6\" of the centre of the battlefield; no enemy units are within 6\" of the centre of the battlefield; one or more Imperial Knights units from your Crusade army are wholly within your opponent’s deployment zone."
      },
      "Chivalric Quest§Chivalric Quest": {
        "text": "**Chivalric Quests.** When mustering, if you have no active Quest and your WARLORD is an IMPERIAL KNIGHTS model, swear your Knights to one of the four Quests and keep its tally for your next three battles. After three battles consult the Tally Rewards of the Quest (4–6 tally marks: 1 Chivalric point; 7–10: 2 Chivalric points; 11+: 3 Chivalric points; fewer than 4: Dishonoured) and allocate the Chivalric points to your pilots in the Update Crusade Cards step. Fewer than four tally marks, or abandoning a Quest, makes your Crusade force **Dishonoured**: you cannot swear a new Quest until you complete the Death Before Dishonour Agenda.\n\n**Pilots.** Every IMPERIAL KNIGHTS model (not EPIC HEROES) has a pilot with a Sworn Alignment; Questor Imperialis and Questor Mechanicus pilots never fight in the same army. The first time a pilot is allocated Chivalric points, select a Mastery no other pilot has (Clarion: TITANIC only; Joust: Questor Imperialis; Mechanisms: Questor Mechanicus; Execution: Freeblade). Levels of Honour: Aspiring 1–3, Esteemed 4–6, Virtuous 7+ Chivalric points; an ARMIGER pilot holds at most 6 points. A pilot with a Mastery adds 1 to the unit's Crusade points. A Knight without a pilot is vacant and cannot be fielded; an unseated pilot can be assigned to a new or vacant Knight (a Virtuous pilot or one with Mastery of the Clarion never to an ARMIGER)."
      }
    },
